# Test: ze delete agent skill agent all, after a create, at a shell
# QUESTION: after `ze create agent skill agent claude`, does
# `ze delete agent skill agent all` remove the ze stub skill it wrote and leave
# another skill beside it, and does `ze show agent skill` then report the stub
# as missing?
# VALIDATES: spec-ze-agent-skill-setup AC-19 (the stub half), AC-18.
# PREVENTS: a delete that answers removed and leaves the stub, or that removes
# a skill Ze did not write.
#
# Method: every child runs in the test's own work directory, so HOME and the
# two harness variables point inside it and nothing reaches the home of whoever
# runs the suite. No daemon runs: the plain local handler answers at a shell.
# The other skill is written by the test itself before the create.

option=env:var=HOME:value=.
option=env:var=CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.claude
option=env:var=CODEX_HOME:value=.codex
option=env:var=XDG_CONFIG_HOME:value=.config

tmpfs=.claude/skills/other/SKILL.md:terminator=EOF_OTHER
---
name: other
description: a skill Ze did not write
---
The operator's own skill.
EOF_OTHER

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze create agent skill agent claude:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze delete agent skill agent all:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=removed

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze show agent skill agent claude:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=missing

expect=file:path=.claude/skills/ze/SKILL.md:absent=true
expect=file:path=.claude/skills/other/SKILL.md:contains=The operator's own skill.
